From 1054f30cf982f5b94977b6f9662cdb0619c3d584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mystic Builder Dev <dev@mysticbuilder.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:11:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Re-add weapon bonds to legendary weapons

Legendary weapons can again bond another weapon, with the bond pool
limited to weapons of the same type and element (e.g. an Umbral Axe
bonds other Umbral Axes):

- Awakening loadout: the Bonded slot row is now always shown for
  bond-capable weapons (it previously only rendered when a bond was
  already stored in the build code, so there was no way to add one)
- Bondable pools in the loadout picker, random builds and the legacy
  build editor now match type + element and exclude the weapon itself
  (previously: any legendary weapon of the same element, including the
  equipped weapon)
- Switching weapons re-validates the bond and clears it when the new
  weapon is not bond-capable or the type/element no longer match
- The bonded weapon's unique effect now renders in the weapon detail
  card below the legendary ability (bonding grants the partner's UE
  and innate perk, like in game); effect text falls back to the
  non-surged variant when no surged variant exists
